      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "As a teenager, Elon Musk went through an existential crisis, reading religion and philosophy in search of the meaning of life\n\nThen he discovered Douglas Adams' The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\n\n“I ended up reading The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, which is actually a book on philosophy, just sort of disguised as a silly humor book. But it's actually a philosophy book. And Adams makes the point that it's actually the question that is harder than the answer”\n\nA seemingly silly humor book helped a teenager searching for meaning realize something profound\n\nFinding the right question is often harder than finding the answer\n\nAnd that curiosity never left him\n\nToday, it's driving him to build rockets, explore the universe, and push humanity toward the stars",
      "quote": null,
